        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-11T16:13:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a good question. I\u0027m not sure why it ignores the WAKE pin, it probably can be configured to accept the WAKE pin. Functionally, we get wake interrupts because we keep the GPIO banks that contain the lid open, power btn, and AC present inputs clocked while in deep sleep. So, on any of those events, the GPIO module triggers an interrupt. But, it\u0027s probably more power efficient to disable those GPIO clocks and instead turn this wake pin interrupt on.",
      "parentUuid": "3e15442f_5c0ef14c",
      "revId": "dc8cb825acc20c9d4bc303cfd4548b2a7c76a4f5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "de23489b_79e0a344",
        "filename": "common/system_common.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 573,
