        "id": 1000016
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-11T15:23:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I personally hate those kind of accessors : For me, that\u0027s just a blatant un-optimization.\nAs we are not doing Java for Enterprise, why not just using the global variable sleep_mask ?",
      "revId": "dc8cb825acc20c9d4bc303cfd4548b2a7c76a4f5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e15442f_9c5b69fb",
        "filename": "common/system_common.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 573,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-11T15:46:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As long as it\u0027s clearly commented:\n\n/* Current sleep mask.  You may read from this variable, but must NOT modify it; use enable_sleep() or disable_sleep() to do that. */\n\nOtherwise someone will decide to modify it directly and won\u0027t use an atomic operation, and that\u0027ll introduce a subtle timing-dependent bug.\n\nIf we make sleep_mask global, wouldn\u0027t it also be better to make enable_sleep() and disable_sleep() inline functions (implementation in header)?\n\nNormally I don\u0027t like direct use of mutable globals because it encourages spaghetti coding, but since the sleep mask is modified in interrupt handlers the performance benefit might be worth it.",
      "parentUuid": "de23489b_79e0a344",
      "revId": "dc8cb825acc20c9d4bc303cfd4548b2a7c76a4f5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe0e4c27_97f58466",
        "filename": "common/system_common.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 573,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-11T16:13:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would lean away from a global variable for a couple reasons. As Randall said, someone may try to set it directly, instead of using atomic set. Also, maybe this function should be renamed to system_is_sleep_allowed(), or something like that. In the future sleep may be blocked due to some other reason, and there\u0027s no reason other functions need to worry about that, they just need to know if sleep is allowed right now. \n\nHowever, you guys know the code better than I do, if you think the performance benefit is more important here, then I can change it. It\u0027s a small difference either way.",
      "parentUuid": "3e15442f_9c5b69fb",
      "revId": "dc8cb825acc20c9d4bc303cfd4548b2a7c76a4f5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
